      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Postsynaptic defects in this important pathway for regulating heart rate and contractile force may contribute to the etiology and pathogenesis of congestive cardiac failure. Such defects may involve the beta-adrenergic receptor, its associated G protein, or adenylate cyclase. Current knowledge about these components of transmembrane cardiac signaling is reviewed."},
